{
  "spec": "docs/models/crafting-slots-spec.md",
  "about": "The contract between the slot model (tools/crafting_helper/slot_model.py) and the engine's parity test (tests/slots.rs). Each case is an abstract item, its ordered targets and what each v2 blueprint must preview on it, as the model computes it from the spec. A modifier's alias is the engine table's key; 'junk' is a modifier that is not a target; a level is the modifier level. A step is goal, resolved side (null when the step has none), currency as written and omens resolved in the order the action lists them; a removal also says whether it is certain to take a non-target. A rejection is its kind as the engine serialises it. Never edit an expectation to match the engine: a difference is settled by the spec.",
